{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>את קרבנו</b> — The term את in the passage about the offering of a ruler is a רבוי (inclusion), teaching that he brings an offering of oil and greatness, because every day he eats delicacies, so that his table not be full while his master's table is empty. Regarding goats: it is written שעיר עזים זכר for a male and שעירת עזים נקבה for a female, because in the name there is no distinction between male and female — all are called עז — therefore one must specify זכר or נקבה. But כבש has a distinction in its name: כבש for a male, כבשה for a female."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The phrase 'ושלחן רבו ריקם' is obscure; rendered hyper-literally as 'his master's table [is] empty,' though the referent of 'רבו' is uncertain and the passage may be textually difficult. 'פטומות' rendered as 'delicacies.'"}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:34.424523692Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}